## Bug Description

When using a CJK input method (Chinese/Japanese/Korean IME) in the desktop composer, the send button does not appear while typing — even after characters have been committed to the input. The voice button remains visible instead of switching to the send button. Typing a punctuation character forces the button to appear as a workaround.

## Root Cause

In `apps/desktop/src/app/chat/composer/index.tsx`, the `handleEditorInput` handler intentionally skips all draft state updates while `composingRef.current` is `true` (during IME composition):

\`\`\`js
const handleEditorInput = (event) => {
  if (composingRef.current) {
    return  // skip during IME composition
  }
  const nextDraft = composerPlainText(editor)
  aui.composer().setText(nextDraft)
  ...
}
\`\`\`

This is correct — reading preedit text mid-composition would be noisy. However, `onCompositionEnd` only resets the flag without flushing the committed text into the draft state:

\`\`\`js
onCompositionEnd={() => {
  composingRef.current = false
  // ← no draft flush here
}}
\`\`\`

The code relies on a subsequent `input` event to do the flush, but that event is not guaranteed to fire on every platform/IME combination. As a result, `draft` stays empty after `compositionend`, so `hasComposerPayload` remains `false` and `showVoicePrimary` stays `true` — the send button never appears.

## Fix

Flush the draft explicitly in `onCompositionEnd`:

\`\`\`js
onCompositionEnd={() => {
  composingRef.current = false
  const editor = editorRef.current
  if (editor) {
    const nextDraft = composerPlainText(editor)
    if (nextDraft !== draftRef.current) {
      draftRef.current = nextDraft
      aui.composer().setText(nextDraft)
    }
  }
}}
\`\`\`

This ensures the send button appears immediately after each IME commit, regardless of whether a follow-up `input` event fires.

## Steps to Reproduce

1. Open the desktop app and start a new chat session.
2. Switch system input to a CJK IME (e.g. macOS Pinyin).
3. Type any Chinese/Japanese/Korean characters and commit them via the IME.
4. Observe: the send button does not appear; only the voice button is shown.
5. Type any punctuation character — the send button appears.

## Environment

- Platform: macOS
- Input method: macOS built-in Pinyin / any CJK IME
